{"subjectId":"java","id":"control-flow","title":"Conditionals & Loops","group":"Core Language: Strings, Arrays & Methods","order":12,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>if</code>/<code>else</code>, the ternary operator and four loop forms — plus labeled <code>break</code>/<code>continue</code> for nested loops.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-git-branch\"></i>if / else if / else</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    static String grade(int score) {\n        if (score &gt;= 90) return \"A\";\n        else if (score &gt;= 75) return \"B\";\n        else if (score &gt;= 50) return \"C\";\n        else return \"F\";\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(grade(95) + grade(80) + grade(60) + grade(10));\n        int n = 7;\n        String parity = (n % 2 == 0) ? \"even\" : \"odd\";     // ternary: an expression\n        System.out.println(n + \" is \" + parity);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>ABCF\n7 is odd</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Conditions must be <code>boolean</code> — <code>if (x = 5)</code> or <code>if (n)</code> do not compile in Java (unlike C). The one sneaky exception: <code>if (flag = true)</code> compiles for a <code>boolean flag</code> and is always true.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-repeat\"></i>Loops at a glance</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Loop</th><th>Syntax</th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>for</code></td><td><code>for (int i = 0; i &lt; n; i++)</code></td><td>You need the index or a counted range</td></tr><tr><td>enhanced <code>for</code></td><td><code>for (T x : arrayOrIterable)</code></td><td>Visiting every element, read-only</td></tr><tr><td><code>while</code></td><td><code>while (cond) { … }</code></td><td>Unknown number of iterations; may run 0 times</td></tr><tr><td><code>do-while</code></td><td><code>do { … } while (cond);</code></td><td>Body must run <strong>at least once</strong> (menus, retries)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        for (int i = 0, j = 10; i &lt; j; i += 3, j -= 3)       // several variables\n            System.out.print(i + \":\" + j + \" \");\n        System.out.println();\n\n        int[] nums = {3, 1, 4};\n        int sum = 0;\n        for (int x : nums) sum += x;\n        System.out.println(\"sum=\" + sum);\n\n        int n = 1234, digits = 0;\n        while (n &gt; 0) { n /= 10; digits++; }\n        System.out.println(\"digits=\" + digits);\n\n        int k = 100;\n        do { System.out.println(\"runs once, k=\" + k); } while (k &lt; 10);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>0:10 3:7\nsum=8\ndigits=4\nruns once, k=100</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-player-skip-forward\"></i>break, continue &amp; labels</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        for (int i = 1; i &lt;= 10; i++) {\n            if (i % 2 == 0) continue;      // skip evens\n            if (i &gt; 7) break;              // stop the loop\n            System.out.print(i + \" \");\n        }\n        System.out.println();\n\n        int[][] grid = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}, {7, 8, 9}};\n        outer:\n        for (int r = 0; r &lt; grid.length; r++) {\n            for (int c = 0; c &lt; grid[r].length; c++) {\n                if (grid[r][c] == 5) {\n                    System.out.println(\"found at \" + r + \",\" + c);\n                    break outer;           // leaves BOTH loops\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>1 3 5 7\nfound at 1,1</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-bug\"></i>Common mistakes</h3>\n<ul><li>Off-by-one: <code>i &lt;= arr.length</code> → <code>ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException</code>. Use <code>i &lt; arr.length</code>.</li><li>Modifying the loop variable inside an enhanced <code>for</code> does nothing to the array — <code>x</code> is a copy.</li><li>Removing from a <code>List</code> inside a for-each throws <code>ConcurrentModificationException</code> — use an <code>Iterator</code> or <code>removeIf</code>.</li><li>A stray <code>;</code> — <code>for (…);</code> or <code>while (…);</code> makes an empty body.</li><li>Floating-point loop counters (<code>for (double d = 0; d != 1; d += 0.1)</code>) may never terminate.</li></ul>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is the difference between while and do-while?</summary><div><p><code>while</code> checks the condition first, so the body may run zero times. <code>do-while</code> checks after the body, so it always runs at least once.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do you break out of nested loops?</summary><div><p>Put a label on the outer loop (<code>outer:</code>) and use <code>break outer;</code> (or <code>continue outer;</code>). Alternatives: move the loops into a method and <code>return</code>, or use a flag variable.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Can the ternary operator replace every if/else?</summary><div><p>No — it is an <em>expression</em> that must produce a value of a common type; it can't contain statements. Use it for simple value choices; nested ternaries hurt readability.</p></div></details></section>"}